design:
Use the already-present exact authority tuple to select the candidate join before the full fold gate:

- for authenticated carriers, select by parent/event plus exact invoke-id, then confirm child-id and spawned-id against that join;
- retain the existing full attempt-token validation after selection;
- for unstamped, malformed, or unknown carriers, use only a bounded diagnostic path that produces stable rejection evidence and never guesses an owner;
- preserve region-prefix behavior and the public event grammar.

Do not require globally unique logical child IDs across independent regions and do not add a second routing registry.

Carry exact join authority through one framework-owned, recordable causal-envelope fact rather than relying solely on event metadata:

- preserve the public completion event value and closed grammar;
- attach the private authority before enqueue so the eventual parent dispatch receives it through the existing event/cofx recording and replay path;
- make direct :dispatch and nested :dispatch-later :event use the same transport;
- remove the obsolete :dispatch-n special case;
- allow metadata only as an immediate internal handoff if it is lifted into the recordable envelope before queueing;
- validate missing/tampered/superseded authority through the existing typed stale policy, never a silent replay-success no-op.

Do not expose a new application control surface, add a second replay channel, or recursively interpret arbitrary/custom effects.

Linearize token validation and cache publication against frame destruction/replacement through the existing incarnation/drain serialization authority.

At minimum:

- compare the live registry token inside the cache publication decision;
- never let an older-token reader replace a newer-token cache entry;
- revalidate the chosen bundle/token before returning;
- retry or fail through the canonical destroyed-frame path if authority changed.

Prefer the existing frame-incarnation synchronization seam. Do not add a second global coordinator or retain dead incarnations.

Extract or reuse one side-effect-free subscription metadata normalizer shared by public `reg-sub` and `lower-inline-sub`. It should:

- validate retired and unknown registration keys under the existing dev/prod policy;
- validate `:sensitive` and `:large` classification values through the canonical classification contract;
- strip production-only documentation fields exactly as public registration does;
- preserve namespaced extension keys and omitted-versus-explicit-nil semantics;
- install runtime-owned slots (`:handler-fn`, `:input-kind`, `:input-signals`) after normalization so metadata cannot override them;
- avoid mutating the global registrar during image assembly.

Do not add an inline-only validator or a compatibility shim. One canonical normalization seam is the simplest correct shape.

