## Problem

PR #5782 catalogues `:rf.error/observation-on-change-failed` in Spec 009, but the promised normative integration is incomplete.

`spec/Spec-Schemas.md` states that every error/warning catalogue category has a required per-category schema, yet this category has no schema row. `spec/006-ReactiveSubstrate.md` describes observation notification/disposal timing but omits the newly load-bearing failure contract: per-lease containment, typed versus untyped handling, exact-one visibility, reporting before registrar/Future boundaries swallow the escape, complete sibling drain, and first-escape rethrow afterward. Spec 009 links readers toward Spec 006, but the target section does not define those semantics.

This leaves rf2-6ui49w's explicit Spec 006/009 acceptance criterion unmet and permits runtime fields/channel behavior to drift without a schema gate. The final schema must follow the resolved exact-once/two-channel fixes rather than freezing the currently defective double-emission shape.

## Required correction

After the runtime emission provenance and two-channel/source-coordinate repairs settle, add the canonical `:rf.error/observation-on-change-failed` schema to Spec-Schemas and amend Spec 006's observation callback/disposal clauses to define:

- which callback boundaries are contained;
- canonical typed, already-emitted typed, malformed-id, and untyped behavior;
- exactly one always-on record and the debug diagnostic counterpart;
- subscription-owned attribution fields and source coordinate;
- full sibling-drain ordering and original first-escape propagation;
- HMR/disposed parity and advanced-production trace elision.

Reconcile Spec 009's row/cross-links with that text. Add or extend a structural catalogue-to-schema check so removing the row or drifting required fields fails. Do not invent a second schema vocabulary or change runtime behavior in this docs slice.

## Proof discipline

Before the fix, exact-ID search returns no match in Spec-Schemas or Spec 006. Afterward, schema validation must exercise the actual runtime record shape from HMR/disposed fixtures and reject missing/wrong channel/attribution fields.

PR #6303 correctly replaced Shadow's timestamp-derived `[:shadow.build/build-info :compiled]` set with re-frame.ui's analyzer-pass compile witness, but active implementation and executable-test comments still teach the retired authority.

The production namespace docstring in `compiler/build_hook.clj:55` first says the timestamp set is deliberately not used, then says the later-hook gap is closed by "the finish-time marker and Shadow's compile record". Several live fixtures in `compiler_digest_carrier_jvm_test.clj` repeat the contradiction:

- lines 280-288 call `:cached false` plus a fresh `:js` object "Shadow's causal per-source compile evidence";
- lines 321-323 and 385-387 say the manually driven source is in Shadow's causal `::build-info :compiled` record;
- lines 636-638 say the marker plus that record distinguish a genuine compile;
- lines 777-784 say the current verdict consults Shadow's causal compile record;
- line 809 says `finish` is not told compilation via `::build-info` even though the helper now causally drives the installed analyzer pass and never writes that set.

These are current authority comments, not archaeology: one is the implementation overview and the others sit beside live tests/mutation explanations, exactly where a programmer or coding agent will learn the mechanism. They directly contradict the new production contract and can cause the timestamp authority to be reintroduced. Reconcile this bounded comment cluster only; runtime and tests are already green and correct.

PR #5955 removed obsolete ui.test/frame and render {:app-db ...} grammar from four spec surfaces, but active v1-required Spec 004C still teaches the removed API at:
- spec/004C-Roots-and-Mount.md lines 494-497: {:frame f} XOR {:app-db v}
- lines 503-509: plan-bearing forms reject {:frame}/{:app-db}
- confirmation register lines 547-548

The shipped ui.test/render opts are closed to :frame, :props, and :sub-overrides. A test-owned frame is minted with the canonical rf/make-frame grammar and :initial-events; render no longer has an :app-db construction door. Spec 004C declares itself v1-required and authoritative for the root/mount contract, so this is active programmer/AI drift, not historical text.

Make a surgical prose reconciliation to the same one-grammar rule as Specs 004/008/009/API. Do not reopen the removed convenience or broaden the render API.

